          "type": "turn",
          "question": "Is there a link between sleep and migraine?",
          "answer": "There is a recognized link between sleep and migraine. Sleep and migraine influence each other in both directions. Disturbed sleep can increase the likelihood of migraine attacks, while migraine attacks can disrupt sleep. Changes in sleep patterns, such as getting too little sleep or sleeping in, are frequently reported as triggers for migraine attacks. This is why many people experience headaches after a late night followed by a long sleep-in, as this shift in sleep timing can provoke an attack (source: \"Sleep and migraine: regularity, and the relationship running both ways\").\n\nI could not cover specific treatment options or detailed management strategies for migraines related to sleep issues. If you need information on those aspects, please consult a healthcare provider.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
